**Version:** `filmcraft-cli 0.2.1` and FilmCraft.app 0.2.1 (macOS universal release builds), macOS 27.2, Apple M1 Pro. Possibly the same root cause as #108, but this one needs no HE-AAC: a plain **AAC-LC** source reproduces it whenever its sample rate differs from the sequence's.

## Summary

When an imported clip's audio is AAC-LC at a sample rate other than the sequence rate, the clip's audio is corrupted in every export: samples reach about 4 to 8 times full scale, which plays as loud crackle and spikes over the original sound. The same audio as PCM WAV, or as MP3, at the same mismatched rate exports cleanly. Setting the sequence's sample rate to match the source also exports cleanly.

`file.newSequence` defaults to 48000 Hz, so any 24, 32 or 44.1 kHz AAC clip placed in a default sequence is affected. Found with a 32 kHz AAC-LC phone-style video clip; reproduced below with generated tones.

## Repro

```sh
# 6 s, 440 Hz tone, AAC-LC 32 kHz stereo (ffmpeg native encoder)
ffmpeg -f lavfi -i "sine=f=440:r=32000:d=6" -f lavfi -i "color=c=gray:s=320x240:r=24:d=6" \
  -filter_complex "[0]volume=0.5,aformat=channel_layouts=stereo[a]" -map 1 -map "[a]" \
  -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p -c:a aac -ar 32000 tone32k.mp4

cat > repro.jsonl <<EOF2
{"id":"file.newProject","params":{"name":"repro"}}
{"id":"file.import","params":{"paths":["$PWD/tone32k.mp4"]}}
{"id":"file.newSequence","params":{"name":"s","width":320,"height":240,"fps":24}}
{"id":"timeline.place","params":{"item":1,"seconds":0}}
{"id":"file.exportMedia","params":{"path":"$PWD/out48.mp4","format":"h264","wait":true}}
{"id":"file.exportMedia","params":{"path":"$PWD/out48.wav","format":"wav","wait":true}}
{"id":"sequence.settings","params":{"sampleRate":32000}}
{"id":"file.exportMedia","params":{"path":"$PWD/out32.mp4","format":"h264","wait":true}}
EOF2
filmcraft-cli --compact run repro.jsonl
```

Every step returns `"ok":true`. The default sequence is 48000 Hz (`sequence.inspect` → `settings.sample_rate`).

