## Summary

Changing a clip's Hard Limiter Look-Ahead Time does not change its anticipation window. The effect accepts 0–30 ms and defaults to 7 ms, but processing uses a fixed 5 ms window. Users cannot select the advertised transient-limiting behavior. The limiter still limits peaks, and Maximum Amplitude still changes the output.

