The signed Exp-Golomb reader/writer have three related boundary failures:

- `write_se(i32::MIN)` panics with `attempt to multiply with overflow` in a development/test build.
- `read_se` accepts codeNum `2^32 - 1`, which maps to `+2147483648`, and returns `Ok(-2147483648)` instead of rejecting the out-of-range result.
- codeNum `2^32`, which maps to the representable value `i32::MIN`, is rejected because `read_se` first narrows codeNum through `read_ue() -> u32`.

ITU-T H.264 (08/2024), section 9.1.1 / Table 9-3, defines the signed mapping. [Public specification](https://www.itu.int/rec/dologin_pub.asp?id=T-REC-H.264-202408-I%21%21PDF-E&lang=e&type=items).

