### Summary

The **Time and Pitch** folder only has one effect, `pitch_shifter`, which changes pitch **without** changing duration. There is no time-stretch effect, so there is no way to change a clip's speed while keeping its pitch — the two halves of the feature never meet:

- Changing a clip's **Speed** (Clip Speed / Duration, `TrackItem.speed`) is plain varispeed resampling, so pitch shifts with it. Doubling the speed raises the audio an octave.
- The **Pitch Shifter** effect can correct pitch afterwards, but it is a separate manual step, it is limited to ±12 semitones, it costs an FFT-frame of latency, and it does not follow the clip's speed automatically.

In Premiere this is Elastic Audio / Time Stretch. In practice the common cases — speeding up a VO line to fit, slowing a dialogue line down, fixing a clip whose source was recorded at the wrong speed — all need *speed change + pitch preserved* as a single operation, and today that is not expressible.

Related: the shuttle-only pitch correction is still buggy and reported separately as #1468 and #2110.

